<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - June 4.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - June 4.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the arrival schedule for major steel scrap vessels unloading at South Korean ports of Inchon, Pusan, Masan, Pohang, Kwangyang and Asan, as detailed on Wednesday by South Korean surveyors.</p>
<p>Steel scrap cargoes</p>
<p>-- INCHON PORT</p>
<p> VESSEL	    TONNE    ETA	  ETD	  BUYER</p>
<p> Grande	    45,000   May  26    June  6    Inchon</p>
<p> Xingsuhai	 35,208   June  1    June 13    Inchon</p>
<p> Rova		38,391   June 20		   Inchon</p>
<p>-- PUSAN PORT</p>
<p> Delta-Trident   35,000   June 11		   Dongkuk</p>
<p>-- MASAN PORT</p>
<p> Venus	     39,185   June 15		   KISCO</p>
<p>-- POHANG PORT</p>
<p> Nurten Ana	33,000   May 25     June 10    Kangwon</p>
<p> Quatetdla	 22,500   End of June	     POSCO</p>
<p>-- KWANGYANG PORT</p>
<p> Feng Yao	  50,000   July 15		   POSCO</p>
<p> Caspian-Trident 35,000   July 24		   POSCO</p>
<p>-- ASAN PORT</p>
<p> Orhan Ekinci    33,474   June 15		   Hanbo</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5650</p>
